-# The span of the table above, as the `Cp` gene's declared bounds. Written here
-# so the gene cannot be bounded somewhere the target function can reach — or,
-# worse, somewhere it cannot, which would make the acceptance bar unreachable
-# by construction at one end of the speed range.
-CP_GENE_BOUNDS = (PRISMATIC_BY_FROUDE[0][1], PRISMATIC_BY_FROUDE[-1][1])
+# THE CEILING IS DELIBERATELY ABOVE THE TABLE, and that is a design decision
+# rather than a drift. 2026-08-23.
+#
+# The floor is still the table's, so the gene cannot go finer than any speed
+# asks for. The CEILING is not, and the reason is that the table answers a
+# different question from the one the gene has to span: `prismatic_target` is
+# the RESISTANCE-optimal Cp at a Froude number, and a houseboat is not a
+# resistance-optimal object. It is a rectangle that floats, and its owner will
+# trade knots for floor area every time.
+#
+# MEASURED, and this is why the number moved. A 16.0 x 4.0 m inland liveaboard
+# with the full ends a barge needs (r_transom 0.92, r_stem 0.70) has a
+# REACHABLE Cp range of 0.831 .. 0.979 — the SAC of a box simply has that much
+# prismatic. Against the old ceiling of 0.710 the kernel refused outright:
+#
+#     sac: Cp 0.7100 unreachable at x_mb 0.550, r_transom 0.920
+#
+# So the barge was not a hull the grammar drew badly; it was one the CP GENE
+# forbade, and the refusal named a Cp the designer had not chosen. Three
+# separate bounds each independently prevented a houseboat (this one, the
+# transom ceiling, and the absent stem gene) and all three have moved.
+#
+# WHAT DOES NOT CHANGE: `prismatic_target` is still the one relation, still
+# the acceptance bar, and a hull above the table still MISSES it — `certify`
+# reports "delivered Cp NNN misses the mission target NNN beyond tolerance"
+# and grades the design MARGINAL. That is the correct outcome: the trade is
+# declared and measured, not hidden. There is no prismatic row in
+# `evaluate.CONSTRAINT_NAMES`, so this widens what may be PROPOSED without
+# softening anything that is enforced.
+BARGE_CP_CEILING = 0.95
+CP_GENE_BOUNDS = (PRISMATIC_BY_FROUDE[0][1], BARGE_CP_CEILING)
 
 
